2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000002843693254?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000172317753194 '''Elin Jakobsdotter Baat, (1578 - 1645)'''] Levnadsbeskrivning. Their daughter Margareta who was born in 1602 in
2 CONC  Eskilsäter / S. & died in 1673 in Steneby / P. To Dingelvik and Högen, Steneby.  Margaret became widow in 1636, when her husband died in Verben, Saxony, during the 30-year war. She then inherited the farm Dingelvik in Steneby. Th
2 CONC e real owner, however, was her mother, Elin Jacobsdotter Bååt, until about 1646. In 1655 Mrs. Margareta took the rescue man Högen to the courtyard, and in 1656 both Northern and Southern Dingelvik and Högen were reported as her fa
2 CONC rmhouses. In addition, she owned the Sword Village, and from 1664 also Hälgerud. During her lifetime, she provided the children with seat yards. She had 8 children. (Sources: The book "Steneby", the book "Ärtemark-en Dalslandssock
2 CONC en" by I Löfgren)
2 CONT * [https://runeberg.org/anrep/4/0302.html '''Lennart (son of Peder, Tab. 4), to Sätra in Wermland; Cavalry captain. The names of his son and daughters, as well as the spouses and descendants of the successors, are recorded in an i
